<Layout title="Privacy — RAW vs JPEG" description="How this photography tool handles your calculator inputs, browser requests and external links."><article class="wrap prose"><p class="eyebrow">PRIVACY & DATA</p><h1>Your photos stay yours.</h1><p class="lead">The site has no photo uploads, user accounts or payment forms.</p><h2>Calculator inputs</h2><p>Storage calculations run in your browser. The site does not send your file sizes, photo counts or pricing assumptions to an application server. Inputs are not saved by this application after you close or reload the page.</p><h2>Cookies and analytics</h2><p>The current site code does not set cookies, use local storage or load analytics or advertising scripts.</p><h2>Website delivery</h2><p>Your browser requests pages, scripts and sample images from the hosting service. Normal website delivery exposes network information such as your IP address and requested URL to that service. Hosting-level logging and security processing are separate from the local calculator.</p><h2>External links</h2><p>Sample downloads, licensing information and the project repository lead to external websites. Those services have their own data practices. There are no active affiliate links in this version.</p><h2>Questions or corrections</h2><p><a href="https://github.com/COLDDCC/raw-vs-jpeg/issues">Contact the project through GitHub Issues ↗</a>. Issues are public: do not include private photographs, credentials or personal information.</p></article></Layout>
